    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d33">

                <pb facs="0057" n="45" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg45"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">890H.24/154: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Afghanistan</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kabul</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-02-11T19:00:00+04:00">February 11,
                            1944—7 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received February 15—9:23 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>19. Afghan authorities urge that a separate shipping quota be established for
                    United States exports to Afghanistan and that within this quota Afghan
                    representatives themselves be permitted to assign priorities for shipment of
                    goods licensed for export by the United States.</p>
                <p>British Legation inclines to view that this would simplify procedure without
                    depriving India of any significant tonnage and without interfering with control
                    by export license. Beecroft<anchor n="2" xml:id="d33-f1"/> and I concur. Joint
                    screening would of course remain necessary here both for preliminary
                    determination of source of supply and to estimate total shipping program.</p>
                <p>British Legation is consulting its Government.</p>
                <p>Please inform FEA.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d33-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d33-f1" n="2" xml:id="d33-f1-content">
                <p>Eric Beecroft of the Office of the Special Representative of the Foreign Economic
                    Administration at New Delhi was at Kabul January 12 to February 13 studying the
                    Afghan supply situation.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d33-f2" n="3" xml:id="d33-f2-content">
                <p>Foreign Economic Administration.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
